{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493547-first-edition-clanbooks-worth-picking-up","id":1493547,"title":"first edition clanbooks, worth picking up?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-22T18:22:24-07:00","id":1493547,"title":"first edition clanbooks, worth picking up?","content":"so! my group and i are playing 5th edition and i have all of the revised clanbooks but i'm curious, is there any material in the first edition clanbooks that make them worth getting, at this point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T18:44:58-07:00","id":1493550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493547-first-edition-clanbooks-worth-picking-up#post1493547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so! my group and i are playing 5th edition and i have all of the revised clanbooks but i'm curious, is there any material in the first edition clanbooks that make them worth getting, at this point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I liked them a lot. They do reflect the slightly different, often more mysterious, atmosphere which existed back in first and second edition. If you\u2019re a stickler for the metaplot, then much of the material of that era predates it, if different, or was in the early stages of creating it. Some of the earliest ones reflect a sort of wacky flavor of first edition - like the Malkavian Clan Book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T19:00:43-07:00","id":1493552,"title":"","content":"I've always liked all the clanbooks, regardless of edition. I'd recommend any of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T22:06:45-07:00","id":1493562,"title":"","content":"Yep, definitely worth getting them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T22:16:29-07:00","id":1493563,"title":"","content":"They are totally worth it<br /> Actuall I think the things in them were not retconned just tweaked in later editions, so they are part of the given Clan's &quot;history and Lore&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T23:15:34-07:00","id":1493565,"title":"","content":"Clan nosferatu stands out. The only one i warn against is Clan ventrue....its a little trippy and genrally non canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 09-23-2022, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T23:24:32-07:00","id":1493566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493547-first-edition-clanbooks-worth-picking-up?p=1493565#post1493565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clan nosferatu stands out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll second that. Loremaster Horrace's (I believe his name was) account of the origin of the Antes was hysterical ... and slightly informative.<br /> <br /> V<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;They do say, Mrs. M, that verbal insults hurt more than physical pain. They are of course wrong, as you will soon discover when I stick this toasting fork into your head.&quot;<br /> <br /> --E. Blackadder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24273-vincent","name":"Vincent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24273_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T02:11:46-07:00","id":1493570,"title":"","content":"I liked some of them more than others, but there aren't really any that are completely useless. Most of them were pretty forgettable, however, I think. <br /> <br /> I seem to remember that I really liked the Giovanni and Nosferatu books. <br /> <br /> In general, though, the Revised Clan Books were much better, if a bit more boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/387-caldorian","name":"Caldorian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T04:50:12-07:00","id":1493573,"title":"","content":"Lasombra, Giovanni, and Nosferatu are stand outs.<br /> <br /> Ravnos is very much in the same vein of racist stereotypes mixed with made up fantasy BS as WoD: Gypsies. Its only real saving grace is some nice artwork.<br /> <br /> The bulk of Assamites is derived entirely from a single nonfiction book about the real-world Assassins cult. And the majority of the interior art is Xerox scans of weapons, so it doesn't even have that going for it. Unless you have a fascination with the Web of Knives cult, it is very skippable.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce is largely responsible for the clan's shift from creepy weirdos to torture pr0n fetishists.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates#post1387573\">My thread where I look at clanbook templates is here.</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 09-23-2022, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T06:18:06-07:00","id":1493574,"title":"","content":"I think they're neat to look at, more in the sense of a time capsule of what early VtM was like than anything you'd actually use. Most of them contained ideas or concepts that were later pulled back or ignored entirely in later editions. The Malkavian clanbook has some examples of that. Ultimately the important stuff appeared in the later revised clanbooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T09:43:59-07:00","id":1493583,"title":"","content":"The original <b>Clanbook: Malkavian</b> feels like ground zero for Fishmalks, fascinating as a historical document but best kept a good distance from the gaming table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T10:37:03-07:00","id":1493585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493547-first-edition-clanbooks-worth-picking-up?p=1493583#post1493583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original <b>Clanbook: Malkavian</b> feels like ground zero for Fishmalks, fascinating as a historical document but best kept a good distance from the gaming table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. There's a few good ideas in it, particularly among the templates, but it's not one of the better ones. The art, especially, does it no favors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T12:39:27-07:00","id":1493593,"title":"","content":"While it has some interesting tidbits, I'm particularly offended by Clanbook: Malkavian. It gave early bless to fishmalks and overall is very prone to usual prejudices about mental health. But then, those clanbooks are precisely form the age when the more ignoble aspects of the early setting were at their apex.<br /> <br /> Is it worth? Depends a lot. They're fun to read and have lots of ideas and concepts that you can use in some way. If you like to rummage through early stuff for ideas to work upon or to glimpse the first drafts of the setting, then sure, they're gold. But they won't really work as effective additions to the <i>current</i> setting, or mechanics (anything remotely useful was already updated since).<br /> <br /> Anything that hasn't been improved or retconned out of existence will need a lot of work to use and/or is of extremely questionable taste. It won't make them useless, but add to the work for adapting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T14:10:55-07:00","id":1493597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493547-first-edition-clanbooks-worth-picking-up?p=1493583#post1493583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original <b>Clanbook: Malkavian</b> feels like ground zero for Fishmalks, fascinating as a historical document but best kept a good distance from the gaming table.</div> </div> </div> </div>There were things in early books that were dropped. Like in Clanbook Malkavian it mentions an alliance between Malkavians and Ragabash werewolves (The Lunatic Fringe I believe it was called) where members get together to play pranks on everyone else. That, understandably, never got mentioned again in any future sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> And speaking of pranks, those were a pretty big thing in the first edition Malkavian clanbook. But it was one of those ideas that proved to be better on paper than on practice. Malkavian pranksters ended up causing massive problems at the gaming table when a player would decide to prank the Prince, or prank other player characters, cause massive disruptions to the chronicle and then defend it by saying, &quot;I'm just playing in character!&quot; As a result, the idea of Malkavians engaging in pranks was largely toned down in later editions and has basically vanished entirely from the current gameline because of how disruptive that facet of them proved to be at the table.<br /> <br /> And this is true for most of the other First Edition clanbooks. There's material in them that was never mentioned in subsequent books, so it's cool to read and see that stuff, but there was probably a good reason for why that stuff didn't appear in future books. Personally I enjoy the first edition Malkavian clanbook because of how wild it is, and I think it's worth reading just for that, but yeah, I wouldn't recommend using much, if anything from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T16:20:40-07:00","id":1493605,"title":"","content":"I liked the Nosferatu, Tremere, Giovanni, Gangrel, and Lasombra Clanbooks quite a bit. Some of the others weren\u2019t quite as good. The Malkavian Clanbook may have caused the most trouble since it did really lean into the fishmalk thing. There were aspects of the book that I liked too, but yeah it went way overboard on the silliness. The Ravnos Clanbook was a lot like the Gypsy book in many regards, so also problematic. <br /> <br /> After the metaplot became really solidified in Revised edition, I didn\u2019t like it as much. In in 1st and 2nd, it was more free form, more mysterious, and that is reflected in many of those early Clanbooks, which is why I liked them. The Gangrel Clanbook had a passage about a Gangrel who lived among lupines, clearly written by someone who had not read W:tA which was coming out about the same time. The interactions between the Gangrel and werewolves in that book were actually a lot more interesting to me than the interactions that would come to be standard - instant death for the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-24T10:07:35-07:00","id":1493638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493547-first-edition-clanbooks-worth-picking-up#post1493547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so! my group and i are playing 5th edition and i have all of the revised clanbooks but i'm curious, is there any material in the first edition clanbooks that make them worth getting, at this point?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is always something of worth in the early editions of the clan books. Be it npcs or character concepts that might inspire you or contradictory lore that might spark a story idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-25T18:00:49-07:00","id":1493694,"title":"","content":"i think i have settle don getting a few (but, also, both of the malkavian books look just awful and i'm wondering if there was something better re: them after the clanbooks?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-26T04:23:33-07:00","id":1493711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493547-first-edition-clanbooks-worth-picking-up?p=1493694#post1493694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i think i have settle don getting a few (but, also, both of the malkavian books look just awful and i'm wondering if there was something better re: them after the clanbooks?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think that about the revised version?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-28T21:26:19-07:00","id":1493947,"title":"","content":"There's also V20's Lore of the Clans, and I think it is well worth it despite not being the best of V20. It works well as both intro and update on their shenanigans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T15:05:48-07:00","id":1493996,"title":"","content":"Among other things, V20: Lore of the Clans gives some quality of life improvements to the game. Like giving Ventrue an actual mechanism for changing their feeding preference. Or giving Assamite Viziers and Sorcerers alternate, thematic Quietus powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}